  "scope": "FamiliarManager, Familiar, BurdenBeast, BurdenContainerListener, Forager, FamiliarSpecial, Pet, Pets, PetDetails, Plugin and CloseEvent compiled unchanged on JDK 11 with JSON-simple 1.1.1 and the published ConstLib 1.4.28 (the Sounds and Items names used checked against their suffixes). Original text inserted into stand-ins at generation time: WeaponInterface.STYLE_DEFENSIVE, the Skills ids, the Log constants, ItemConfigParser.BANKABLE and Location.getDistance (transcribed to Java beside it). Everything else is a recording stand-in answering from the case: the NPC and entity members (each node keeps its location, visibility, ids and attributes), the player's managers (skills, packet dispatch, interfaces, dialogue, appearance, quests, skull, zones, locks, combat pulse, pulse manager), containers, item and NPC definitions, ContentAPI, RegionManager.getSpawnLocation, GameWorld (ticks and the pulser), RandomFunction, Projectile, BattleState, CombatSwingHandler, SummoningPouch, SummoningScroll, SkillcapePerks and the packet repository. The content classes of the corpus (CaseFamiliar, CaseBeast, CaseForager) extend the unchanged classes and record construct, specialMove, getIds, configureFamiliar, getText, handleFamiliarTick, adjustPlayerBattle and getRandom. Each case runs in a class loader of its own.",
